      "standard_id": "MIASE",
      "name": "Minimum Information About a Simulation Experiment (MIASE)",
      "description": "A minimum-information reporting guideline for computational simulation experiments. Specifies the essential metadata required to reproduce and interpret a simulation experiment, including the models used, any model modifications, the sequence of simulation steps, algorithms and their parameterization/numerical settings, inputs and initial conditions, outputs and post-processing procedures, and software/environment details. Intended as a checklist for documenting simulation experiments to enable reproducibility."
    }
